.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt PAGER_SUPPLY 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm pager_supply
.Nd supply a page to a pager-backed memory object
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Fn pager_supply object offset data data_len
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
supplies one page of
.Fa data
to the pager-backed memory object
.Fa object
created with
.Fn memobj_create len flags
and the
.Dv memobj::PAGER
flag.
The caller must be the object's registered pager.
.Fa offset
is page-aligned and inside the object;
.Fa data_len
is between 1 and the page size.
The kernel copies the bytes into a fresh frame, marks the page present and wakes
threads waiting on that page.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Zero on success; a negative
.Va errno
on failure.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Er EBADF
.Fa object
is not a live memory object.
.It Er EPERM
The caller is not the object's pager.
.It Er EINVAL
The offset, length or range is invalid.
.It Er EFAULT
The data pointer is not readable.
.It Er ENOMEM
No frame is available.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr memobj_create 2 ,
.Xr map 2
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1, contract C18.
